{"id":"mahabharata-3-002","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":2,"title":"द्वितीयोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 2 · Shaunaka's teaching on detachment","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira grieves that he cannot feed the Brahmins who follow him. The sage Shaunaka teaches him that wealth and desire bring sorrow, and that a wise man is untouched by grief, and advises him to win his wish by austerity.","kn":"ಹಿಂಬಾಲಿಸುವ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರಿಗೆ ಅನ್ನ ಹಾಕಲಾರೆನೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ದುಃಖಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಧನ ಕಾಮಗಳು ದುಃಖ ತರುತ್ತವೆ, ಜ್ಞಾನಿಯನ್ನು ಶೋಕ ಸೋಕದು ಎಂದು ಶೌನಕ ಋಷಿ ಉಪದೇಶಿಸಿ ತಪಸ್ಸಿನಿಂದ ಇಷ್ಟಾರ್ಥ ಪಡೆಯೆಂದು ಸಲಹೆ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर दुःखी हैं कि वे साथ आए ब्राह्मणों को भोजन नहीं दे सकते। ऋषि शौनक उन्हें सिखाते हैं कि धन और कामना दुःख लाते हैं, ज्ञानी को शोक नहीं छूता, और सलाह देते हैं कि तप से अपना मनोरथ पूरा करें।","te":"వెంట వచ్చిన బ్రాహ్మణులకు భోజనం పెట్టలేనని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు దుఃఖిస్తాడు. ధనం, కామం దుఃఖాన్ని తెస్తాయని, జ్ఞానిని శోకం తాకదని శౌనక ఋషి ఉపదేశించి తపస్సుతో కోరిక తీర్చుకొమ్మని సలహా ఇస్తాడు.","ta":"பின்தொடரும் அந்தணர்களுக்கு உணவளிக்க முடியவில்லையே என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் வருந்துகிறார். செல்வமும் ஆசையும் துயரம் தரும், ஞானியைத் துயரம் தீண்டாது என்று ஶௌனக முனிவர் உபதேசித்து, தவத்தால் விருப்பத்தை அடையுமாறு அறிவுரை சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"തന്നെ പിന്തുടരുന്ന ബ്രാഹ്മണർക്ക് ഭക്ഷണം നൽകാനാവാത്തതിൽ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ദുഃഖിക്കുന്നു. സമ്പത്തും ആഗ്രഹവും ദുഃഖം നൽകുന്നുവെന്നും ജ്ഞാനിയെ ദുഃഖം ബാധിക്കില്ലെന്നും ശൗനകൻ പഠിപ്പിക്കുന്നു; തപസ്സിലൂടെ ആഗ്രഹം നേടാൻ അദ്ദേഹം ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.2; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"आरण्यकपर्व","titleEn":"Aranyaka Parva (Into the forest)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रभातायां तु शर्वर्यां तेषामक्लिष्टकर्मणाम् ।\nवनं यियासतां विप्रास्तस्थुर्भिक्षाभुजोऽग्रतः ।\nतानुवाच ततो राजा कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When dawn came, as those men of untroubled deeds prepared to go to the forest, the Brahmins who lived on alms stood before them. King Yudhishthira, Kunti's son, then spoke to them."}},{"n":2,"text":"वयं हि हृतसर्वस्वा हृतराज्या हृतश्रियः ।\nफलमूलामिषाहारा वनं यास्याम दुःखिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have lost everything: our kingdom, our fortune and our glory. Grieving, we shall go to the forest living on fruit, roots and game."}},{"n":3,"text":"वनं च दोषबहुलं बहुव्यालसरीसृपम् ।\nपरिक्लेशश्च वो मन्ये ध्रुवं तत्र भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The forest is full of dangers, with many beasts and serpents, and I think hardship will surely befall you there."}},{"n":4,"text":"ब्राह्मणानां परिक्लेशो दैवतान्यपि सादयेत् ।\nकिं पुनर्मामितो विप्रा निवर्तध्वं यथेष्टतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Brahmin's hardship could shake even the gods; how much more me. Brahmins, turn back from here as you wish."}},{"text":"ब्राह्मणा ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The Brahmins said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"गतिर्या भवतां राजंस्तां वयं गन्तुमुद्यताः ।\nनार्हथास्मान्परित्यक्तुं भक्तान्सद्धर्मदर्शिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, we are ready to go wherever your path leads. You should not abandon devoted followers who see the true dharma."}},{"n":6,"text":"अनुकम्पां हि भक्तेषु दैवतान्यपि कुर्वते ।\nविशेषतो ब्राह्मणेषु सदाचारावलम्बिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the gods show kindness to their devotees, and especially to Brahmins who hold to right conduct."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"ममापि परमा भक्तिर्ब्राह्मणेषु सदा द्विजाः ।\nसहायविपरिभ्रंशस्त्वयं सादयतीव माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins, my devotion to Brahmins is also supreme and constant. But this loss of my helpers weighs me down."}},{"n":8,"text":"आहरेयुर्हि मे येऽपि फलमूलमृगांस्तथा ।\nत इमे शोकजैर्दुःखैर्भ्रातरो मे विमोहिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even my brothers, who would bring me fruit, roots and game, are bewildered by the pains born of sorrow."}},{"n":9,"text":"द्रौपद्या विप्रकर्षेण राज्यापहरणेन च ।\nदुःखान्वितानिमान्क्लेशैर्नाहं योक्तुमिहोत्सहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are afflicted by Draupadi's humiliation and the loss of the kingdom; I cannot bear to add more hardship to them."}},{"text":"ब्राह्मणा ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The Brahmins said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"अस्मत्पोषणजा चिन्ता मा भूत्ते हृदि पार्थिव ।\nस्वयमाहृत्य वन्यानि अनुयास्यामहे वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, let no worry about feeding us trouble your heart. We will gather forest food ourselves and come along."}},{"n":11,"text":"अनुध्यानेन जप्येन विधास्यामः शिवं तव ।\nकथाभिश्चानुकूलाभिः सह रंस्यामहे वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"We will work for your welfare by meditation and prayer, and we will delight together with you in the forest with pleasant stories."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"एवमेतन्न संदेहो रमेयं ब्राह्मणैः सह ।\nन्यूनभावात्तु पश्यामि प्रत्यादेशमिवात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is surely so, without doubt, and I would delight in the company of Brahmins. But in my poverty I see a kind of rebuke to myself."}},{"n":13,"text":"कथं द्रक्ष्यामि वः सर्वान्स्वयमाहृतभोजनान् ।\nमद्भक्त्या क्लिश्यतोऽनर्हान्धिक्पापान्धृतराष्ट्रजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can I watch you all fetch your own food, troubled for love of me, undeserving of it? Shame on Dhritarashtra's wicked sons!"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा स नृपः शोचन्निषसाद महीतले ।\nतमध्यात्मरतिर्विद्वाञ्शौनको नाम वै द्विजः ।\nयोगे सांख्ये च कुशलो राजानमिदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So saying, the king sat down on the ground in grief. Then the Brahmin Shaunaka, learned, devoted to the Self and skilled in yoga and Sankhya, spoke to him."}},{"n":15,"text":"शोकस्थानसहस्राणि भयस्थानशतानि च ।\nदिवसे दिवसे मूढमाविशन्ति न पण्डितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thousands of occasions for grief and hundreds for fear enter the fool every day, but not the wise man."}},{"n":16,"text":"न हि ज्ञानविरुद्धेषु बहुदोषेषु कर्मसु ।\nश्रेयोघातिषु सज्जन्ते बुद्धिमन्तो भवद्विधाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Intelligent men like you do not cling to actions that are contrary to knowledge, full of faults and destructive of one's good."}},{"n":17,"text":"अष्टाङ्गां बुद्धिमाहुर्यां सर्वाश्रेयोविघातिनीम् ।\nश्रुतिस्मृतिसमायुक्तां सा राजंस्त्वय्यवस्थिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"They speak of an eight-limbed intelligence that destroys all that is harmful and is joined with the Veda and tradition. That, king, is in you."}},{"n":18,"text":"अर्थकृच्छ्रेषु दुर्गेषु व्यापत्सु स्वजनस्य च ।\nशारीरमानसैर्दुःखैर्न सीदन्ति भवद्विधाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men like you do not sink in troubles over wealth, in difficulties, or in calamities to their kin, nor under pains of body and mind."}},{"n":19,"text":"श्रूयतां चाभिधास्यामि जनकेन यथा पुरा ।\nआत्मव्यवस्थानकरा गीताः श्लोका महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen to the verses that the great-souled Janaka once sang, which give steadiness to the self."}},{"n":20,"text":"मनोदेहसमुत्थाभ्यां दुःखाभ्यामर्दितं जगत् ।\nतयोर्व्याससमासाभ्यां शमोपायमिमं शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"The world is tormented by two sorrows, of mind and of body. Hear, in brief and in detail, the means to calm them."}},{"n":21,"text":"व्याधेरनिष्टसंस्पर्शाच्छ्रमादिष्टविवर्जनात् ।\nदुःखं चतुर्भिः शारीरं कारणैः संप्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bodily pain arises from four causes: disease, contact with the unwelcome, exertion, and being deprived of what one wants."}},{"n":22,"text":"तदाशुप्रतिकाराच्च सततं चाविचिन्तनात् ।\nआधिव्याधिप्रशमनं क्रियायोगद्वयेन तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Quick remedy and not brooding constantly calm both mental and bodily illness; this is done by two practices."}},{"n":23,"text":"मतिमन्तो ह्यतो वैद्याः शमं प्रागेव कुर्वते ।\nमानसस्य प्रियाख्यानैः संभोगोपनयैर्नृणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So wise physicians first calm the mind, with pleasant talk and the offering of enjoyments to people."}},{"n":24,"text":"मानसेन हि दुःखेन शरीरमुपतप्यते ।\nअयःपिण्डेन तप्तेन कुम्भसंस्थमिवोदकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The body is scorched by mental sorrow, like water in a pot over a heated iron ball."}},{"n":25,"text":"मानसं शमयेत्तस्माज्ज्ञानेनाग्निमिवाम्बुना ।\nप्रशान्ते मानसे दुःखे शारीरमुपशाम्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"So one should quench the mind's fire with knowledge as with water. When mental sorrow is calmed, bodily sorrow subsides."}},{"n":26,"text":"मनसो दुःखमूलं तु स्नेह इत्युपलभ्यते ।\nस्नेहात्तु सज्जते जन्तुर्दुःखयोगमुपैति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The root of the mind's sorrow is found to be attachment. Through attachment a creature clings, and through it comes to sorrow."}},{"n":27,"text":"स्नेहमूलानि दुःखानि स्नेहजानि भयानि च ।\nशोकहर्षौ तथायासः सर्वं स्नेहात्प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sorrows have attachment as their root, and fears are born of attachment. Grief, joy and weariness all proceed from attachment."}},{"n":28,"text":"स्नेहात्करणरागश्च प्रजज्ञे वैषयस्तथा ।\nअश्रेयस्कावुभावेतौ पूर्वस्तत्र गुरुः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From attachment come passion of the senses and craving for objects; both are harmful, and the first is held the weightier."}},{"n":29,"text":"कोटराग्निर्यथाशेषं समूलं पादपं दहेत् ।\nधर्मार्थिनं तथाल्पोऽपि रागदोषो विनाशयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a fire in a hollow burns up a whole tree to its roots, so even a small fault of passion destroys one who seeks dharma."}},{"n":30,"text":"विप्रयोगे न तु त्यागी दोषदर्शी समागमात् ।\nविरागं भजते जन्तुर्निर्वैरो निष्परिग्रहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who renounces does not turn away merely by parting; seeing the fault in union, a creature grows dispassionate, free of enmity and possessions."}},{"n":31,"text":"तस्मात्स्नेहं स्वपक्षेभ्यो मित्रेभ्यो धनसंचयात् ।\nस्वशरीरसमुत्थं तु ज्ञानेन विनिवर्तयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So one should turn away by knowledge from attachment to one's own side, friends, hoarding of wealth, and even to one's own body."}},{"n":32,"text":"ज्ञानान्वितेषु मुख्येषु शास्त्रज्ञेषु कृतात्मसु ।\nन तेषु सज्जते स्नेहः पद्मपत्रेष्विवोदकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among the foremost who are full of knowledge, versed in the scriptures and self-controlled, attachment does not cling, as water does not cling to lotus leaves."}},{"n":33,"text":"रागाभिभूतः पुरुषः कामेन परिकृष्यते ।\nइच्छा संजायते तस्य ततस्तृष्णा प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man overcome by passion is dragged along by desire. Wish arises in him, and from that thirst follows."}},{"n":34,"text":"तृष्णा हि सर्वपापिष्ठा नित्योद्वेगकरी नृणाम् ।\nअधर्मबहुला चैव घोरा पापानुबन्धिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thirst is the worst of all sins, always bringing men unrest; it is full of unrighteousness, dreadful, and linked to evil."}},{"n":35,"text":"या दुस्त्यजा दुर्मतिभिर्या न जीर्यति जीर्यतः ।\nयोऽसौ प्राणान्तिको रोगस्तां तृष्णां त्यजतः सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fools cannot give it up and it does not age even as one ages; it is a disease lasting to life's end. Those who abandon that thirst find happiness."}},{"n":36,"text":"अनाद्यन्ता तु सा तृष्णा अन्तर्देहगता नृणाम् ।\nविनाशयति संभूता अयोनिज इवानलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That thirst, without beginning or end, lodged within men's bodies, destroys them once it arises, like a fire that has no womb."}},{"n":37,"text":"यथैधः स्वसमुत्थेन वह्निना नाशमृच्छति ।\nतथाकृतात्मा लोभेन सहजेन विनश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"As firewood is destroyed by the fire arising from itself, so a man of unrefined self perishes through his own inborn greed."}},{"n":38,"text":"राजतः सलिलादग्नेश्चोरतः स्वजनादपि ।\nभयमर्थवतां नित्यं मृत्योः प्राणभृतामिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wealthy always fear the king, water, fire, thieves and even their own kin, as living beings fear death."}},{"n":39,"text":"यथा ह्यामिषमाकाशे पक्षिभिः श्वापदैर्भुवि ।\nभक्ष्यते सलिले मत्स्यैस्तथा सर्वेण वित्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As meat is eaten by birds in the sky, beasts on earth and fish in water, so the rich man is devoured by everyone."}},{"n":40,"text":"अर्थ एव हि केषांचिदनर्थो भविता नृणाम् ।\nअर्थश्रेयसि चासक्तो न श्रेयो विन्दते नरः ।\nतस्मादर्थागमाः सर्वे मनोमोहविवर्धनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For some men wealth itself becomes ruin. A man bound to the pursuit of wealth does not find the good. So all ways of acquiring wealth increase the mind's delusion."}},{"n":41,"text":"कार्पण्यं दर्पमानौ च भयमुद्वेग एव च ।\nअर्थजानि विदुः प्राज्ञा दुःखान्येतानि देहिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise know that miserliness, pride and arrogance, fear and anxiety are the sorrows that wealth brings to embodied beings."}},{"n":42,"text":"अर्थस्योपार्जने दुःखं पालने च क्षये तथा ।\nनाशे दुःखं व्यये दुःखं घ्नन्ति चैवार्थकारणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is sorrow in earning wealth, in guarding it, in its decline, in its loss, and in spending it; and men kill for wealth's sake."}},{"n":43,"text":"अर्था दुःखं परित्यक्तुं पालिताश्चापि तेऽसुखाः ।\nदुःखेन चाधिगम्यन्ते तेषां नाशं न चिन्तयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wealth is a sorrow to give up, an unhappiness even when guarded, and hard to gain. One should not grieve at its loss."}},{"n":44,"text":"असंतोषपरा मूढाः संतोषं यान्ति पण्डिताः ।\nअन्तो नास्ति पिपासायाः संतोषः परमं सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fools are bent on discontent; the wise attain contentment. Thirst has no end; contentment is the highest happiness."}},{"n":45,"text":"तस्मात्संतोषमेवेह धनं पश्यन्ति पण्डिताः ।\nअनित्यं यौवनं रूपं जीवितं द्रव्यसंचयः ।\nऐश्वर्यं प्रियसंवासो गृध्येदेषु न पण्डितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the wise see contentment alone as wealth in this world. Youth, beauty, life, hoards of goods, power and living with loved ones are all impermanent; the wise man should not crave them."}},{"n":46,"text":"त्यजेत संचयांस्तस्मात्तज्जं क्लेशं सहेत कः ।\nन हि संचयवान्कश्चिद्दृश्यते निरुपद्रवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So one should give up hoards. Who would bear the pain they cause? No man with hoards is ever seen free from trouble."}},{"n":47,"text":"अतश्च धर्मिभिः पुम्भिरनीहार्थः प्रशस्यते ।\nप्रक्षालनाद्धि पङ्कस्य दूरादस्पर्शनं वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore righteous men praise freedom from striving for wealth. It is better to keep far from mud than to wash it off."}},{"n":48,"text":"युधिष्ठिरैवमर्थेषु न स्पृहां कर्तुमर्हसि ।\nधर्मेण यदि ते कार्यं विमुक्तेच्छो भवार्थतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, you should not crave wealth. If you want to act by dharma, free yourself from desire for wealth."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":49,"text":"नार्थोपभोगलिप्सार्थमियमर्थेप्सुता मम ।\nभरणार्थं तु विप्राणां ब्रह्मन्काङ्क्षे न लोभतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, this wish for wealth is not for craving enjoyment. I want it to support the Brahmins, not out of greed."}},{"n":50,"text":"कथं ह्यस्मद्विधो ब्रह्मन्वर्तमानो गृहाश्रमे ।\nभरणं पालनं चापि न कुर्यादनुयायिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could one like me, living in the householder's stage, fail to support and look after his dependents?"}},{"n":51,"text":"संविभागो हि भूतानां सर्वेषामेव शिष्यते ।\nतथैवापचमानेभ्यः प्रदेयं गृहमेधिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"A share is due to all creatures; likewise a householder must give to those who cannot cook for themselves."}},{"n":52,"text":"तृणानि भूमिरुदकं वाक्चतुर्थी च सूनृता ।\nसतामेतानि गेहेषु नोच्छिद्यन्ते कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grass, ground, water and, fourth, pleasant speech are never lacking in the homes of the good."}},{"n":53,"text":"देयमार्तस्य शयनं स्थितश्रान्तस्य चासनम् ।\nतृषितस्य च पानीयं क्षुधितस्य च भोजनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should give a bed to the afflicted, a seat to the tired traveler, water to the thirsty and food to the hungry."}},{"n":54,"text":"चक्षुर्दद्यान्मनो दद्याद्वाचं दद्याच्च सूनृताम् ।\nप्रत्युद्गम्याभिगमनं कुर्यान्न्यायेन चार्चनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should offer a welcoming glance, a kind mind and pleasant words, go forth to meet a guest, and honor him properly."}},{"n":55,"text":"अघिहोत्रमनड्वांश्च ज्ञातयोऽतिथिबान्धवाः ।\nपुत्रदारभृताश्चैव निर्दहेयुरपूजिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unhonored, the sacred fire, the ox, one's relatives, guests, kinsmen, and one's wife, children and dependents can burn one up."}},{"n":56,"text":"नात्मार्थं पाचयेदन्नं न वृथा घातयेत्पशून् ।\nन च तत्स्वयमश्नीयाद्विधिवद्यन्न निर्वपेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not cook food for oneself alone, nor needlessly kill animals, nor eat oneself what one has not offered in the proper way."}},{"n":57,"text":"श्वभ्यश्च श्वपचेभ्यश्च वयोभ्यश्चावपेद्भुवि ।\nवैश्वदेवं हि नामैतत्सायंप्रातर्विधीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should set out food on the ground for dogs, outcastes and birds. This is called the Vaishvadeva offering, prescribed morning and evening."}},{"n":58,"text":"विघसाशी भवेत्तस्मान्नित्यं चामृतभोजनः ।\nविघसं भृत्यशेषं तु यज्ञशेषं तथामृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So one should always eat the remnant, which is like nectar: the remnant left by dependents, and the nectar of the sacrifice's remains."}},{"n":59,"text":"एतां यो वर्तते वृत्तिं वर्तमानो गृहाश्रमे ।\nतस्य धर्मं परं प्राहुः कथं वा विप्र मन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"They call such a way of life, followed in the householder's stage, the highest dharma. What do you think, Brahmin?"}},{"text":"शौनक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shaunaka said:"}},{"n":60,"text":"अहो बत महत्कष्टं विपरीतमिदं जगत् ।\nयेनापत्रपते साधुरसाधुस्तेन तुष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alas, what a great pain; the world is turned upside down, for a good man feels shame at the very thing that pleases the bad."}},{"n":61,"text":"शिश्नोदरकृतेऽप्राज्ञः करोति विघसं बहु ।\nमोहरागसमाक्रान्त इन्द्रियार्थवशानुगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the sake of belly and sex a fool does much unsanctioned eating, overcome by delusion and passion and enslaved to sense objects."}},{"n":62,"text":"ह्रियते बुध्यमानोऽपि नरो हारिभिरिन्द्रियैः ।\nविमूढसंज्ञो दुष्टाश्वैरुद्भ्रान्तैरिव सारथिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even a man who knows is carried away by his captivating senses, bewildered, like a charioteer dragged by vicious, wild horses."}},{"n":63,"text":"षडिन्द्रियाणि विषयं समागच्छन्ति वै यदा ।\nतदा प्रादुर्भवत्येषां पूर्वसंकल्पजं मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the six senses meet their objects, the mind, born of earlier intentions, then rises up among them."}},{"n":64,"text":"मनो यस्येन्द्रियग्रामविषयं प्रति चोदितम् ।\nतस्यौत्सुक्यं संभवति प्रवृत्तिश्चोपजायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a man's mind is turned toward the objects of the senses, eagerness arises in him and activity begins."}},{"n":65,"text":"ततः संकल्पवीर्येण कामेन विषयेषुभिः ।\nविद्धः पतति लोभाग्नौ ज्योतिर्लोभात्पतंगवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, pierced by desire, with the strength of intention and arrows of sense objects, he falls into the fire of greed, as a moth falls into a flame."}},{"n":66,"text":"ततो विहारैराहारैर्मोहितश्च विशां पते ।\nमहामोहमुखे मग्नो नात्मानमवबुध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, lord of men, deluded by pleasures and food, he sinks into the mouth of great delusion and does not know himself."}},{"n":67,"text":"एवं पतति संसारे तासु तास्विह योनिषु ।\nअविद्याकर्मतृष्णाभिर्भ्राम्यमाणोऽथ चक्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus he falls in the cycle of rebirth, whirled like a wheel by ignorance, action and thirst, through this or that womb."}},{"n":68,"text":"ब्रह्मादिषु तृणान्तेषु हूतेषु परिवर्तते ।\nजले भुवि तथाकाशे जायमानः पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through all states from Brahma down to a blade of grass, called in turn, he revolves, born again and again in water, on earth and in the sky."}},{"n":69,"text":"अबुधानां गतिस्त्वेषा बुधानामपि मे शृणु ।\nये धर्मे श्रेयसि रता विमोक्षरतयो जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the course of the unwise. Now hear from me the course of the wise, those who delight in dharma and the good, and love liberation."}},{"n":70,"text":"यदिदं वेदवचनं कुरु कर्म त्यजेति च ।\nतस्माद्धर्मानिमान्सर्वान्नाभिमानात्समाचरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Vedic word says both \"do action\" and \"renounce\". So one should perform all these duties without pride."}},{"n":71,"text":"इज्याध्ययनदानानि तपः सत्यं क्षमा दमः ।\nअलोभ इति मार्गोऽयं धर्मस्याष्टविधः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sacrifice, study, giving, austerity, truth, forbearance, self-restraint and freedom from greed: this is called the eightfold path of dharma."}},{"n":72,"text":"तत्र पूर्वश्चतुर्वर्गः पितृयानपथे स्थितः ।\nकर्तव्यमिति यत्कार्यं नाभिमानात्समाचरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of these, the first four lie on the path of the ancestors. One should do what ought to be done, without pride."}},{"n":73,"text":"उत्तरो देवयानस्तु सद्भिराचरितः सदा ।\nअष्टाङ्गेनैव मार्गेण विशुद्धात्मा समाचरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The latter four are the path of the gods, always followed by the good. With the eightfold path, the purified self should act."}},{"n":74,"text":"सम्यक्संकल्पसंबन्धात्सम्यक्चेन्द्रियनिग्रहात् ।\nसम्यग्व्रतविशेषाच्च सम्यक्च गुरुसेवनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rightly through right intention, right restraint of the senses, right observance of vows and right service of the teacher,"}},{"n":75,"text":"सम्यगाहारयोगाच्च सम्यक्चाध्ययनागमात् ।\nसम्यक्कर्मोपसंन्यासात्सम्यक्चित्तनिरोधनात् ।\nएवं कर्माणि कुर्वन्ति संसारविजिगीषवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"right food, right study of the sacred texts, right renunciation of action and right control of thought: so do those who wish to conquer rebirth act."}},{"n":76,"text":"रागद्वेषविनिर्मुक्ता ऐश्वर्यं देवता गताः ।\nरुद्राः साध्यास्तथादित्या वसवोऽथाश्विनावपि ।\nयोगैश्वर्येण संयुक्ता धारयन्ति प्रजा इमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Free from passion and hatred, the gods attained sovereignty: Rudras, Sadhyas, Adityas, Vasus and the two Ashvins. Endowed with yogic power, they sustain these creatures."}},{"n":77,"text":"तथा त्वमपि कौन्तेय शममास्थाय पुष्कलम् ।\nतपसा सिद्धिमन्विच्छ योगसिद्धिं च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"So you too, son of Kunti, take up fully the calm of self-control, and seek success through austerity, and the perfection of yoga, descendant of Bharata."}},{"n":78,"text":"पितृमातृमयी सिद्धिः प्राप्ता कर्ममयी च ते ।\nतपसा सिद्धिमन्विच्छ द्विजानां भरणाय वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have received the perfection that comes from parents and the perfection that comes from action. Seek the perfection of austerity, for the support of the Brahmins."}},{"n":79,"text":"सिद्धा हि यद्यदिच्छन्ति कुर्वते तदनुग्रहात् ।\nतस्मात्तपः समास्थाय कुरुष्वात्ममनोरथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For perfected ones accomplish whatever they wish through their grace. So resort to austerity and fulfil the wish of your heart."}}]}]}